    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store E.164 form, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **New `mapper/E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained helper with one static `toE164` method (WMC_other = 0, no surrounding class complexity to carry). It strips spaces, dashes and brackets; keeps a leading `+` and its country code when present; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits; and requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the existing `normalizeTelephone` hook now delegates in one line to `E164Telephone.toE164(...)`, so the edited method stays trivial (CC 1) rather than absorbing the new logic.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` field's Bean Validation from the old `^[0-9]{10}$` / `@Digits` to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` so the stored E.164 value validates (annotation change, no method touched; removed the now-unused `@Digits` import).\n\n**Behavior:**\n- `0412 345 678` \u2192 stored/returned as `+61412345678`\n- `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456` (explicit country code kept)\n- Unformattable numbers like `12` are rejected with 400 (at the request-DTO validation layer, before mapping).\n- Duplicate detection compares the stored E.164 values \u2014 the existing `OwnerTelephonePolicy` already compares by digits, which is equivalent for two E.164 strings, so it needed no change.",
